next_step: "Apply the requested changes to /Users/olivier/projects/firstmate/data/captain-training-program-s1/program.html. Do not respond to the user just yet. Now you must run `lavish-axi poll /Users/olivier/projects/firstmate/data/captain-training-program-s1/program.html --agent-reply \"<message for the user>\"` without --timeout-ms unless the user ended the session. Keep the reply concise. Only when a longer reply is genuinely necessary, use Markdown structure - blank-line paragraphs, `- ` / `1. ` lists, `## ` headings - so it renders scannably instead of a wall of text, and pass that body with `--agent-reply-file <path>` (`-` reads stdin) so newlines survive quoting. The Conversation panel's Markdown subset is in `lavish-axi poll --help` and README. The poll waits silently until the user sends more feedback, ends the session, or leaves every review window disconnected past the reconnect grace period - never kill it. Keep the poll in the foreground by default and let it return the feedback directly to the agent. A background poll is allowed only through a harness-native tracked background-job facility whose completion result is guaranteed to resume or notify the same agent. Never use `nohup`, shell `&`, `disown`, redirected fire-and-forget processes, or a detached terminal without an explicit verified callback merely to keep polling alive. If the harness has no completion-aware background facility, use the foreground poll or first wire a verified wake callback into the surrounding supervisor. Do not tell the user the artifact is being monitored until that wake path is live. If the poll gets killed or times out before feedback arrives, re-run it - feedback remains queued until delivery. Poll delivery consumes the response, so read it completely. If it returns browser_disconnected, the review window stayed disconnected past its reconnect grace period but the session remains resumable; ask the user whether to reopen or end it, and do neither uninvited."
dom_snapshot: "uid=9 body \"Training program: restart and recomposition Stadium 1, Av. du Sippelberg 1, 1080\"\n  uid=10 main \"Training program: restart and recomposition Stadium 1, Av. du Sippelberg 1, 1080\"\n    uid=11 h1 \"Training program: restart and recomposition\"\n    uid=12 p \"Stadium 1, Av. du Sippelberg 1, 1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean. Height 1.91 m. Goal: \"\n    uid=13 div \"Every number on this page is a starting estimate. Your weight, age and injuries \"\n      uid=14 b \"Every number on this page is a starting estimate.\"\n      uid=15 br\n      uid=16 b \"See a doctor before you start if\"\n      uid=17 span \"(ACSM pre-participation screening, Riebe et al. 2015)\"\n    uid=18 h2 \"Five questions that change the program\"\n    uid=19 div \"What are your age and your weight today? (Waist too, if you know it.) The protei\"\n      uid=20 ol \"What are your age and your weight today? (Waist too, if you know it.) The protei\"\n        uid=21 li \"What are your age and your weight today? (Waist too, if you know it.) The protei\"\n          uid=1 b \"What are your age and your weight today?\"\n        uid=3 li \"Do you have pain or an old injury in the back, knees or shoulders, or a medical \"\n          uid=22 b \"Do you have pain or an old injury\"\n        uid=4 li \"How many days per week and how many minutes per visit can you train? The default\"\n          uid=23 b \"How many days per week and how many minutes per visit\"\n        uid=24 li \"Do you wear an Apple Watch or another wearable, and is your phone an iPhone? Bev\"\n          uid=5 b \"Do you wear an Apple Watch or another wearable, and is your phone an iPhone?\"\n        uid=25 li \"Do you prefer to follow this plan yourself, or to let the gym load it into the a\"\n          uid=6 b \"Do you prefer to follow this plan yourself, or to let the gym load it into the a\"\n    uid=26 nav \"1. The gym: Stadium 1 2. The plan in one view 3. Weeks 1-2: reintroduction 4. We\"\n      uid=27 a \"1. The gym: Stadium 1\"\n      uid=28 br\n      uid=29 a \"2. The plan in one view\"\n      uid=30 br\n      uid=31 a \"3. Weeks 1-2: reintroduction\"\n      uid=32 br\n      uid=33 a \"4. Weeks 3-14: main phase\"\n      uid=34 br\n      uid=35 a \"5. Two-day and four-day variants\"\n      uid=36 br\n      uid=37 a \"6. Progression rules\"\n      uid=38 br\n      uid=39 a \"7. Walking and cardio\"\n      uid=40 br\n      uid=41 a \"8. Nutrition frame\"\n      uid=42 br\n      uid=43 a \"9. Sleep\"\n      uid=44 br\n      uid=45 a \"10. Measure every two weeks\"\n      uid=46 br\n      uid=47 a \"11. Apps: MyStadiumPro + Bevel, no double entry\"\n      uid=48 br\n      uid=49 a \"12. Can an agent read or write your Technogym data?\"\n      uid=50 br\n      uid=51 a \"13. Bevel assessment\"\n      uid=52 br\n      uid=53 a \"14. Sources\"\n    uid=54 h2 \"1. The gym: Stadium 1\"\n    uid=55 p \"You are already a member. Facts below come from the Stadium 1 website (stadiumon\"\n      uid=56 span \"verified\"\n      uid=57 span \"unverified\"\n    uid=58 div \"Opening hours Days Hours Monday to Friday 07:00 - 23:00 verified Saturday and Su\"\n      uid=59 div \"Opening hours Days Hours Monday to Friday 07:00 - 23:00 verified Saturday and Su\"\n        uid=60 h3 \"Opening hours\"\n        uid=61 table \"Days Hours Monday to Friday 07:00 - 23:00 verified Saturday and Sunday 09:00 - 1\"\n          uid=62 tbody \"Days Hours Monday to Friday 07:00 - 23:00 verified Saturday and Sunday 09:00 - 1\"\n            uid=63 tr \"Days Hours\"\n            uid=64 tr \"Monday to Friday 07:00 - 23:00 verified\"\n            uid=65 tr \"Saturday and Sunday 09:00 - 19:00 verified\"\n        uid=66 p \"Holiday hours: unverified. Your Stadium 1 membership also gives access to Stadiu\"\n          uid=67 span \"verified\"\n      uid=68 div \"Coaching and intake Fitness initiation: first visit with a certified 'initiator'\"\n        uid=69 h3 \"Coaching and intake\"\n        uid=70 ul \"Fitness initiation: first visit with a certified 'initiator', by appointment. Th\"\n          uid=71 li \"Fitness initiation: first visit with a certified 'initiator', by appointment. Th\"\n            uid=72 b \"Fitness initiation\"\n            uid=73 span \"verified\"\n            uid=74 span \"unverified\"\n          uid=75 li \"Personal fitness assistance: 30 minutes, €30, for a new or updated plan. verifie\"\n            uid=76 b \"Personal fitness assistance\"\n            uid=77 b \"€30\"\n            uid=78 span \"verified\"\n          uid=79 li \"MyWellness Band: €20. verified\"\n            uid=7 b \"MyWellness Band\"\n            uid=80 span \"verified\"\n          uid=81 li \"Body assessment results appear in the app. verified What the assessment measures\"\n            uid=82 span \"verified\"\n            uid=83 span \"unverified\"\n    uid=84 div \"Equipment on the floor Area What the gym states Status Technogym strength and ca\"\n      uid=85 h3 \"Equipment on the floor\"\n      uid=86 table \"Area What the gym states Status Technogym strength and cardio machines 'Latest T\"\n        uid=87 tbody \"Area What the gym states Status Technogym strength and cardio machines 'Latest T\"\n          uid=88 tr \"Area What the gym states Status\"\n            uid=89 th \"Area\"\n            uid=90 th \"What the gym states\"\n            uid=91 th \"Status\"\n          uid=92 tr \"Technogym strength and cardio machines 'Latest Technogym technology', a wide ran\"\n            uid=93 td \"Technogym strength and cardio machines\"\n            uid=94 td \"'Latest Technogym technology', a wide range of cardio and strength machines.\"\n            uid=95 td \"verified Exact models: unverified\"\n          uid=96 tr \"Biostrength (Technogym) New AI strength machines. They set load, speed, range an\"\n            uid=97 td \"Biostrength (Technogym)\"\n            uid=98 td \"New AI strength machines. They set load, speed, range and rest, and record every\"\n            uid=99 td \"verified Which stations: unverified\"\n          uid=100 tr \"Biocircuit (Technogym) 30-minute circuit: 6 strength machines + 2 cardio machine\"\n            uid=101 td \"Biocircuit (Technogym)\"\n            uid=102 td \"30-minute circuit: 6 strength machines + 2 cardio machines. The machines adjust \"\n            uid=103 td \"verified\"\n          uid=104 tr \"CrossTraining room (functional area) 'Extensive' room with kettlebells, jump rop\"\n            uid=105 td \"CrossTraining room (functional area)\"\n            uid=106 td \"'Extensive' room with kettlebells, jump ropes, dumbbells; squats, push-ups, pull\"\n            uid=107 td \"verified\"\n          uid=108 tr \"Free weights: dumbbell rack, benches, barbells, squat racks, cable stations Not \"\n            uid=109 td \"Free weights: dumbbell rack, benches, barbells, squat racks, cable stations\"\n            uid=110 td \"Not described on the website.\"\n            uid=111 td \"unverified\"\n          uid=112 tr \"Other Two pools (25 m and 20 m), sauna, hammam, squash, badminton, pickleball, d\"\n            uid=113 td \"Other\"\n            uid=114 td \"Two pools (25 m and 20 m), sauna, hammam, squash, badminton, pickleball, dojo, g\"\n            uid=115 td \"verified\"\n      uid=116 p \"Because the free-weight area is unverified, every exercise below has a machine o\"\n    uid=117 h2 \"2. The plan in one view\"\n    uid=118 table \"Weeks Phase Sessions Effort Main aim 1 - 2 Reintroduction 3 per week, 45 min Eas\"\n      uid=119 tbody \"Weeks Phase Sessions Effort Main aim 1 - 2 Reintroduction 3 per week, 45 min Eas\"\n        uid=120 tr \"Weeks Phase Sessions Effort Main aim\"\n          uid=121 th \"Weeks\"\n          uid=122 th \"Phase\"\n          uid=123 th \"Sessions\"\n          uid=124 th \"Effort\"\n          uid=125 th \"Main aim\"\n        uid=126 tr \"1 - 2 Reintroduction 3 per week, 45 min Easy: stop 3-4 reps before failure Learn\"\n          uid=127 td \"1 - 2\"\n          uid=128 td \"Reintroduction\"\n          uid=129 td \"3 per week, 45 min\"\n          uid=130 td \"Easy: stop 3-4 reps before failure\"\n          uid=8 td \"Learn the machines, find starting weights, no heavy soreness\"\n        uid=131 tr \"3 - 7 Main block 1 3 per week, 50-60 min Moderate: stop 2-3 reps before failure \"\n          uid=132 td \"3 - 7\"\n          uid=133 td \"Main block 1\"\n          uid=134 td \"3 per week, 50-60 min\"\n          uid=135 td \"Moderate: stop 2-3 reps before failure\"\n          uid=136 td \"Add weight every week or two\"\n        uid=137 tr \"8 Easy week 3 per week, half the sets Easy Recover, first re-check of measuremen\"\n          uid=138 td \"8\"\n          uid=139 td \"Easy week\"\n          uid=140 td \"3 per week, half the sets\"\n          uid=141 td \"Easy\"\n          uid=142 td \"Recover, first re-check of measurements\"\n        uid=143 tr \"9 - 13 Main block 2 3 per week, 55-60 min Harder: stop 1-2 reps before failure M\"\n          uid=144 td \"9 - 13\"\n          uid=145 td \"Main block 2\"\n          uid=146 td \"3 per week, 55-60 min\"\n          uid=147 td \"Harder: stop 1-2 reps before failure\"\n          uid=148 td \"More sets, keep adding weight\"\n        uid=149 tr \"14 Test and review 3 per week, normal sets Test top sets Compare with week 3, th\"\n          uid=150 td \"14\"\n          uid=151 td \"Test and review\"\n          uid=152 td \"3 per week, normal sets\"\n          uid=153 td \"Test top sets\"\n          uid=154 td \"Compare with week 3, then plan the next 12 weeks\"\n    uid=155 h3 \"A normal week (3-day default)\"\n    uid=156 div \"Monday Session A + 15-20 min easy bike Tuesday Walk 30-45 min Wednesday Session \"\n      uid=157 div \"Monday Session A + 15-20 min easy bike\"\n        uid=158 b \"Monday\"\n        uid=159 br\n      uid=160 div \"Tuesday Walk 30-45 min\"\n        uid=161 b \"Tuesday\"\n      uid=162 div \"Wednesday Session B + 15-20 min easy bike\"\n        uid=163 b \"Wednesday\"\n      