week, for exa\"\n        uid=289 h3 \"2 days per week (minimum)\"\n        uid=290 ul \"Do Session A and Session B once each per week, for example Monday and Thursday. \"\n          uid=291 li \"Do Session A and Session B once each per week, for example Monday and Thursday.\"\n          uid=292 li \"Exercises 1-4: 3 sets in block 1, 4 sets in block 2. Exercises 5-7: 2-3 sets.\"\n            uid=293 b \"4 sets\"\n          uid=294 li \"Sessions are about 60-70 minutes.\"\n          uid=295 li \"Walk more: target the top of the step range (section 7).\"\n          uid=296 li \"Expect slower muscle gain than with 3 days; fat loss depends mostly on food.\"\n      uid=297 div \"4 days per week A - B - rest - A - B - rest - rest (for example Mon, Tue, Thu, F\"\n        uid=298 h3 \"4 days per week\"\n        uid=299 ul \"A - B - rest - A - B - rest - rest (for example Mon, Tue, Thu, Fri). Exercises 1\"\n          uid=300 li \"A - B - rest - A - B - rest - rest (for example Mon, Tue, Thu, Fri).\"\n          uid=301 li \"Exercises 1-4: 3 sets in both blocks (do not go to 4). Exercises 5-7: 2 sets.\"\n          uid=302 li \"Sessions are about 45-50 minutes.\"\n          uid=303 li \"Use this only when sleep is 7 hours or more and soreness is gone before each ses\"\n    uid=304 h2 \"6. Progression rules (for every exercise)\"\n    uid=305 div \"Double progression. Every exercise has a rep range, for example 8-12. Start with\"\n      uid=306 p \"Double progression. Every exercise has a rep range, for example 8-12.\"\n        uid=307 b \"Double progression.\"\n      uid=308 ol \"Start with a weight where you reach the bottom of the range (8) with the target \"\n        uid=309 li \"Start with a weight where you reach the bottom of the range (8) with the target \"\n        uid=310 li \"Each session, try to add 1 rep per set at the same weight.\"\n        uid=311 li \"When all sets reach the top of the range (12) with the target reps in reserve, i\"\n          uid=312 b \"all sets reach the top of the range (12)\"\n        uid=313 li \"After the increase, the reps fall back towards 8. Repeat.\"\n        uid=314 li \"If the reps go down for 2 sessions in a row at the same weight: check sleep and \"\n          uid=315 b \"down\"\n        uid=316 li \"Plank: add 10 s when you can hold 45 s with good form; at 60 s, go to a harder v\"\n      uid=317 p \"Reps in reserve (RIR) = how many more reps you could do with good form. RIR-base\"\n    uid=318 h2 \"7. Walking and cardio\"\n    uid=319 table \"Weeks Daily steps (weekly average) Cardio at the gym 1 - 2 6,000 - 7,000, or +1,\"\n      uid=320 tbody \"Weeks Daily steps (weekly average) Cardio at the gym 1 - 2 6,000 - 7,000, or +1,\"\n        uid=321 tr \"Weeks Daily steps (weekly average) Cardio at the gym\"\n          uid=322 th \"Weeks\"\n          uid=323 th \"Daily steps (weekly average)\"\n          uid=324 th \"Cardio at the gym\"\n        uid=325 tr \"1 - 2 6,000 - 7,000, or +1,500 above your current average 5-10 min easy warm-up \"\n          uid=326 td \"1 - 2\"\n          uid=327 td \"6,000 - 7,000, or +1,500 above your current average\"\n          uid=328 td \"5-10 min easy warm-up only\"\n        uid=329 tr \"3 - 7 8,000 2 x 15-20 min easy (bike, cross-trainer, incline walk) after Session\"\n          uid=330 td \"3 - 7\"\n          uid=331 td \"8,000\"\n          uid=332 td \"2 x 15-20 min easy (bike, cross-trainer, incline walk) after Sessions A/B. You c\"\n        uid=333 tr \"8 - 14 8,000 - 10,000 2 x 20 min easy. Optional from week 9: replace one with 10\"\n          uid=334 td \"8 - 14\"\n          uid=335 td \"8,000 - 10,000\"\n          uid=336 td \"2 x 20 min easy. Optional from week 9: replace one with 10 x (30 s hard / 90 s e\"\n    uid=337 p \"Target for the week: 150-300 minutes of moderate activity in total (WHO 2020); b\"\n    uid=338 h2 \"8. Nutrition frame\"\n    uid=339 div \"Protein (the most important number) Target: 1.6 g per kg body weight per day; up\"\n      ui